    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201-a2">

                <pb facs="0326" n="238" xml:id="pg238"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Zaldo to Mr. Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Cuba, Department of State and Justice,<lb/>Division of
                                State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February 1, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Squiers</hi>: I am officially commissioned,
                    in the name of the Government, to present to you our most energetic disapproval
                    of the occurrence which has happened at Cienfuegos, of which you informed me in
                    your letter of yesterday.</p>
                <p>We propose that the author of such a low crime, which has greatly pained the
                    Government, shall not remain without punishment.</p>
                <p>I shall have the highest pleasure in transmitting to you the results of our
                    investigations at an opportune moment.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlos de Zaldo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
